ver, from Washington’s perspective, it seems their ground is rooted in the belief that China has taken advantage of them, and therefore they wish to start all negotiations from that point, seeing tariffs as something which came later,” Liu said. Another batch of US tariffs is due to go into effect on December 15, putting an extra 15 per cent on US$156 billion of Chinese goods. China has said it will impose another round of tariffs on US$75 billion worth of US goods – including soybeans – on December 15, in line with the US schedule. This follows a tariff increase in September. Additional reporting by Reuters\",\"articleSection\":\"Diplomacy\",\"author\":{\"name\":\"Kinling Lo\",\"sameAs\":\"https://www.scmp.com/author/kinling-lo\"},\"dateCreated\":\"2019-12-01T12:41:23+08:00\",\"dateModified\":\"2019-12-01T23:01:20+08:00\",\"datePublished\":\"2019-12-01T12:42:39+08:00\",\"genre\":\"News\",\"hasPart\":{\"isAccessibleForFree\":\"False\"},\"headline\":\"Trade deal must include US tariff rollback says China’s Global Times\",\"inLanguage\":\"en-GB\",\"isAccessibleForFree\":\"False\",\"locationCreated\":{\"name\":\"Beijing\"},\"publisher\":{\"name\":\"South China Morning Post\"}}"
